<title>GERMANY: German farm union backs EU in hormone meat ban.</title>
<headline>German farm union backs EU in hormone meat ban.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German farm union DBV said in a statement it backed the European Union's import ban on hormone-treated beef from the United States.</p>
<p>DBV president Gerd Sonnleitner said EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler had his organisation's full backing in maintaining the import ban.</p>
<p>&quot;German and European consumers cannot tolerate the use of growth hormones which stresses animals and may harm human health,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The World Trade Organisation (WTO) recently upheld a U.S. complaint that the EU unfairly barred U.S. meat shipments in the dispute.</p>
<p>The WTO has issued an interim report and both parties have another fortnight to return their comments after which the WTO will issue a formal ruling with view to approval by member countries.</p>
<p>Sonnleitner said if the EU was forced to accept U.S. imports, it should demand origin labelling of beef imports from third countries.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
